15 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Infographic diagram illustrates the evolutionary process of tumors, highlighting tumor initiation, branched clonal evolution, dissemination, metastatic colonization, and therapy resistance. It explains selective pressures like immune, stromal, and treatment factors that influence context-dependent clonal fitness. Multi-omics approaches are shown: lineage tracing, cell state and niche mapping, longitudinal liquid biopsies, and evolutionary inference. The final section outlines clinical applications, including early detection, minimal residual disease monitoring, recurrence prediction, treatment stratification, and adaptive sequencing based on evolutionary data. Validation pathways from analytical to prospective utility are displayed at the bottom.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Infographic summarizing cancer evolution in hepatocellular carcinoma, esophageal squamous cell carcinoma, and gastric cancer, organized by shared evolutionary processes, cancer-specific trajectories, tissue context, molecular anchors, representative findings, and cautions. Includes diagrams of clonal evolution, tissue injury, biomarkers, and distinctions in dissemination, ecological selection, plasticity, and translational opportunities for each cancer type. Text, illustrations, and tables highlight molecular alterations, microenvironmental selection, and therapeutic implications across cancer types.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
